('34122','20','discovery[{#SNMPVALUE},1.3.6.1.4.1.9.9.109.1.1.1.1.5]','10394','CPU discovery','cpu.discovery','1h','90d','0','0','4','','','','',NULL,NULL,'','','0','','','','','1',NULL,'If your IOS device has several CPUs, you must use CISCO-PROCESS-MIB and its object cpmCPUTotal5minRev from the table called cpmCPUTotalTable ,\r\nindexed with cpmCPUTotalIndex .\r\nThis table allows CISCO-PROCESS-MIB to keep CPU statistics for different physical entities in the router,\r\nlike different CPU chips, group of CPUs, or CPUs in different modules/cards.\r\nIn case of a single CPU, cpmCPUTotalTable has only one entry.','0','7d','0','',NULL,'','','','','200','1','0','','','0','0','0','0','0','0','0','f472cb3505b34f14b84bc1ce69f66b29','0','2','0'),
