('44395','20','discovery[{#SNMPVALUE},1.3.6.1.4.1.9.9.109.1.1.1.1.2]','10551','CPU discovery','cpu.discovery','1h','90d','0','0','4','','','','',NULL,NULL,'','','0','','','','','1',NULL,'You must use CISCO-PROCESS-MIB and its object `cpmCPUTotal5minRev` from the table called `cpmCPUTotalTable`, and indexed with `cpmCPUTotalPhysicalIndex`.\r\nThe table `cpmCPUTotalTable` allows CISCO-PROCESS-MIB to keep the CPU statistics for different physical entities in the router, such as different CPU chips, a group of CPUs, or CPUs in different modules/cards.\r\nIn the case of a single CPU, the `cpmCPUTotalTable` has only one entry.','0','7d','0','',NULL,'','','','','200','1','0','','','0','0','0','0','0','0','0','d1d6b8c10e83484e82e37b58c7004d9e','0','2','0'),
