('18444','{$IFCONTROL:"{#IFNAME}"}=1 and {23925}=2 and ({23926}<>{23927})','Mellanox: Interface {#IFNAME}({#IFALIAS}): Link down','','0','3','This trigger expression works as follows:\r\n1. It can be triggered if the operations status is down.\r\n2. `{ $IFCONTROL:"{#IFNAME}" }=1` - a user can redefine context macro to value - 0. That marks this interface as not important. No new trigger will be fired if this interface is down.\r\n3. The trigger fires only if the operational status was up to (1) sometime before (so, do not fire for the \'eternal off\' interfaces.)\r\n\r\nWARNING: if closed manually - it will not fire again on the next poll, because of .diff.',NULL,'0','2','1','{23925}<>2 or {$IFCONTROL:"{#IFNAME}"}=0','0','','1','Current state: {ITEM.LASTVALUE1}','0','','46918cfc713a4b1da7eed32cead0070b',''),
