('25224','{36084}>{$REDIS.MEM.ALLOC_RSS_RATIO.MAX.WARN} and {36085}>{$REDIS.MEM.ALLOC_RSS_BYTES.MIN}','Redis: Allocator RSS ratio is too high','','0','2','Ratio between allocator_resident and allocator_active.\r\nIndicates pages that the allocator can and probably will soon release\r\nback to the OS. If sustained, consider running MEMORY PURGE.',NULL,'0','2','0','','0','','0','','0','Redis: Allocator RSS ratio is too high (over {$REDIS.MEM.ALLOC_RSS_RATIO.MAX.WARN} in 15m)','a6e21d0527bf461f87de7adb81482730',''),
('25225','{36086}>{$REDIS.MEM.ALLOC_FRAG_RATIO.MAX.WARN} and {36087}>{$REDIS.MEM.ALLOC_FRAG_BYTES.MIN}','Redis: Memory allocator fragmentation is too high','','0','2','Memory fragmentation at the allocator level indicates how efficiently the memory allocator is using physical memory:\r\n  - Value over 1.5 means the allocator has significantly more fragmented memory than necessary.\r\n    Consider enabling active defragmentation (activedefrag yes) or restarting Redis to reclaim fragmented memory.\r\n  - Low fragmentation (close to 1.0) is normal and expected.',NULL,'0','2','0','','0','','0','','0','Redis: Memory allocator fragmentation is too high (over {$REDIS.MEM.ALLOC_FRAG_RATIO.MAX.WARN} in 15m)','c0b8bfdb5d2d416094b82011791b55a2',''),
('25226','{36088}>{$REDIS.MEM.RSS_OVERHEAD_RATIO.MAX.WARN} and {36089}>{$REDIS.MEM.RSS_OVERHEAD_BYTES.MIN}','Redis: RSS overhead ratio is too high','','0','2','Ratio between used_memory_rss (the process RSS) and allocator_resident.\r\nIncludes RSS overheads that are not allocator or heap related.\r\nIf sustained, investigate persistence configuration (BGSAVE frequency, AOF rewrite settings).',NULL,'0','2','0','','0','','0','','0','Redis: RSS overhead ratio is too high (over {$REDIS.MEM.RSS_OVERHEAD_RATIO.MAX.WARN} in 15m)','3444356bd5d246e18f5dde9c44d82405','');
